ost commercial preparations. Overall, Vitamin K is a critical nutrient for maintaining health, particularly in relation to blood coagulation and bone health.\",20\r\n2603,COMITÉ DE NUTRICIÓN DE LA AEP,\"The Committee on Nutrition of the AEP provides recommendations for infant nutrition and supplementation, particularly regarding vitamin K and vitamin D for newborns.\",3\r\n3504,HEMORRAGIAS,\"Hemorragias refer to bleeding that can occur within adrenal masses, which may be discovered incidentally during medical examinations. Additionally, hemorrhages can arise from a significant deficiency of vitamin K, a crucial nutrient necessary for proper blood clotting. This highlights the importance of both anatomical factors, such as adrenal masses, and nutritional deficiencies in the occurrence of hemorragias.\",2\r\n11482,ENFERMEDAD DE WHIPPLE,\"La enfermedad de Whipple es una enfermedad infecciosa que afecta la absorción intestinal, lo que puede llevar a deficiencias de magnesio.\",1\r\n15372,FLÚOR,Fluorine is recommended to prevent dental caries and is primarily sourced from drinking water.,2\r\n11483,FÁRMACOS INHIBIDORES DE LA BOMBA DE PROTONES,Los fármacos inhibidores de la bomba de protones son medicamentos que reducen la producción de ácido en el estómago y pueden contribuir a la malabsorción de magnesio.,1\r\n3509,AYUNO PROLONGADO,\"Prolonged fasting can result in deficiencies of vitamins, particularly vitamin K.\",1\r\n13031,HEPATOPATÍA SEVERA,\"Severe liver disease is a condition that may require careful management of vitamin supplementation, particularly Vitamin A and K.\",1\r\n15377,ALIMENTOS RICOS EN FLÚOR,Fluorine is primarily found in drinking water and is important for dental health.,1\r\n\n\n-----Relationships-----\nhuman_readable_id,source,target,description,combined_degree\r\n3401,PACIENTE,HIPOMAGNESEMIA,\"El paciente fue diagnosticado con hipomagnesemia, que se trató con suplementos\",567\r\n4609,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,ENFERMEDAD INFLAMATORIA,Enfermedad infla